# Rock Band Landing Page

## Project Title
Rock Band Landing Page – Events & Promotion

## Description
This project is a responsive landing page designed for a rock band. The main goal is to promote the band’s identity, music, and upcoming events while capturing the attention of potential fans and concert attendees. The design focuses on energy, style, and personality, using visual elements that match the rock genre.

## Technologies Used
- HTML5
- CSS3

## Project Structure
project-folder/  
│  
├── index.html        # Main landing page  
├── css/  
│   └── styles.css   # Stylesheet  
├── img/  
│   └── images       # Images used in the project  
└── README.md        # Project documentation  

## Features
The project includes a semantic HTML structure using tags such as `header`, `nav`, `section`, `article`, and `footer`. It contains a hero section with an impactful design, a section for upcoming events including dates, locations, and cities, and an "about the band" section. It also includes a multimedia section with images or embedded content, as well as organized lists such as musical influences, band values, or social media links. The design follows a rock style with appropriate colors and typography, and it uses Flexbox and/or Grid layout for proper organization.

## Responsive Design
The website is fully responsive and adapts to different screen sizes, including mobile devices and desktop screens (greater than 1024px). Media queries are used to ensure a correct layout across all devices.

## How to Run the Project
To run this project:
1. Download or clone the repository  
2. Open the project folder  
3. Open the `index.html` file in any web browser  

No additional installations are required.

## Purpose
This project was created as part of a frontend development assessment to demonstrate skills in HTML5 structure, CSS3 styling, responsive design, and basic UI/UX principles.
